1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Her date of death was recorded in [https://books.google.com/books?id=BAN6ONlDkgIC&printsec=frontcover&source=gbs_ge_summary_r&cad=0#v=onepage&q&f=false '''The Annals of the Saljuq Turks: Selections from Al-Kamil Fi
2 CONC 'l-Ta'rikh of Ibn Al-Athir'''], translated by D.S. Richards. Here is the passage:
2 CONT
2 CONT This year the mother of the Caliph al-Qa'im bi-Amr Allah died. Her name was Dewdrop (Qatr al-Nada). Some reports say Moon of the Dark (Badr al-Duja) or Banner (Alam). She was an Armenian slave girl.
