1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ruqaiyah bint Muhammad''' Banu Hâshim1
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a dispute about her father. Sunni Muslims believe she was Muhammad's biological daughter. Shi'a Muslims believe she was Muhammad's stepdaughter, daughter of Khadijah by her second marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT She had one son, 'Abdullah, who died in childhood. She had no further children.
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Who were Khadijah's children by her second husband? This is another controversy that revolves round the other daughters or step-daughters of the Prophet (ص) besides Fatima (ع). These daughters, chronologically arranged, are: Zai
2 CONC nab, Ruqayya, and Ummu Kulthoom. Some historians say that these were Khadijah's daughters by her second husband, whereas others insist they were her daughters by Muhammad (ص). The first view is held by Sayyid Safdar Husayn in his 
2 CONC book The Early History of Islam in which he bases his conclusion on the contents of al-Sayyuti's famous work Tarikh al-Khulafa wal Muluk (history of the caliphs and kings; do not confuse it with Tabari's Tarikh; both books bear th
2 CONC e same title, and this is not uncommon at all)." (Al-Jibouri)
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 598, d. 623
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: [http://www.geni.com/people/Prophet-Muhammad-of-Islam-PBUH/6000000000388939419 Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allâh al-Mustafa (pbuh&hf), The Prophet2] b. 9 May 570, d. 8 June 632
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: [http://www.geni.com/people/Khadijah-al-Kubra-r-a/6000000000737643783 Khadîjah bint Khuwaylid banu As'sad al-Qurayshiyya2] b. circa 555, d. between 619 and 620
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruqaiyah bint Muhammad Banu Hâshim was the daughter of Muhammad and Khadijah.1 She was the mother of 'Abd Allâh ibn 'Uthman Banu 'Abd Shams; the son of Ruqaiyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).3 Ruqaiyah bi
2 CONC nt Muhammad Banu Hâshim was born circa 598. She was the daughter of Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allâh al-Mustafa (pbuh&hf), The Prophet and Khadîjah bint Khuwaylid banu As'sad al-Qurayshiyya.2 Ruqaiyah bint Muhammad Banu Hâshim married `Utb
2 CONC ah ibn Abu Lahab Banu Hâshim, son of Clan Chief Abu Lahab ibn 'Abd al-Muttalib Banu Hâshim, before 610; Her 1st. Married in the pre-Islamic period.4,1 Ruqaiyah bint Muhammad Banu Hâshim and `Utbah ibn Abu Lahab Banu Hâshim were di
2 CONC vorced circa 612; When Islam emerged and the Qur'anic verse "May the hands of Abu Lahab perish! May he himself perish" (Surah Al-Masad, Verse 1) was revealed, Abu Lahab told his son to divorce her, the daughter of the Prophet hims
2 CONC elf.1 Ruqaiyah bint Muhammad Banu Hâshim married 'Uthman ibn 'Affan al-Qurayshi, 3rd Rightly Guided Caliph of Islam, son of 'Affan ibn Abûl 'Âs, circa 613; Her 2nd (divorcee).1 Ruqaiyah bint Muhammad Banu Hâshim migrated with her 
2 CONC 2nd husband to Abyssinia at Africa.1 She died in 623 at 2 A.H., Medina.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1
2 CONT
2 CONT `Utbah ibn Abu Lahab Banu Hâshim b. circa 580
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Uthman ibn 'Affan al-Qurayshi, 3rd Rightly Guided Caliph of Islam b. circa 593, d. 17 June 656
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
