2 CONC SIM_7768>
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utba_ibn_Rabi%27ah
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah (Arabic: عتبة بن ربيعة‎) was one of the prominent Leaders of Quraish during the era of Muhammad. (The Quraysh (Arabic: قريش‎, Qurayš; other transliterations include Qureish, Quraish, Quresh, Qurish, Kuraish, and
2 CONC  Coreish) were a powerful merchant tribe that controlled Mecca and its Ka'aba and that, according to Islamic tradition, descended from Ishmael.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The Islamic prophet Muhammad was born into the Banu Hashim clan of the Quraysh tribe
2 CONT
2 CONT Utbah's father was Rabi'ah ibn Abd Shams. Utbah's daughter, Hind bint Utbah, married Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, another of the Leaders of the Quraish and Muhammad's arch-enemy. Utbah had two sons, Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah and Walid ibn U
2 CONC tba, and a brother named Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Utbah was killed in the battle of Badr
