1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Original name '''Hakam ibn Wa'il'''. Also known as '''al-Hakam ibn Abi al-'As'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hakam_ibn_Abi_al-%27As
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Al-Hakam ibn Abi al-`As ibn Umayyah (Arabic: الحكم بن أبي العاص‎ / ALA-LC: al-Ḥakam bin Abī al-‘As) was the father of the Umayyad Caliph Marwan I, and an uncle of Uthman. He is regarded as a Sahabi by Sunnis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hakam was the grandson of Umayya ibn Abd Shams, for whom the Umayyad clan is named. His father was Abu al-'As ibn Umayya. His brother was Affan ibn Abi al-'As the father of Uthman, the third Sunni Caliph, and his son Marwan ibn al
2 CONC -Hakam was the eighth Sunni Caliph.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saffya bint abi al-A'as, al-Hakam's sister, is the aunt of Uthman ibn Affan, the wife of Abu Sufyan, and the mother of Ramlah bint Abi-Sufyan, a wife of Muhammad. He also had brother named Uthman ibn Abi al-'As.
