1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It is now clear that Mu'mine Khatun was the widow of Toghril II of Great Seljuk due to the [https://books.google.com/books?id=16yHq5v3QZAC&pg=PA170&lpg=PA170&dq=Inanj+Sonqur&source=bl&ots=1KiidLPl__&sig=iwp6o97ZkT6
2 CONC PHnw4kRXTDaUE1BE&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwi4h4TvtufOAhUHXhoKHQgOBxEQ6AEINTAE#v=onepage&q=Inanj&f=false '''Cambridge History of Iran, Vol. 5'''], by J.A. Boyle:
2 CONT
2 CONT The north-west provinces of Iran remained quite outside the sultans' sphere of direct influence. Power here was divided between the Eldiguzids and the Ahmadilis. Shams al-Din Eldiguz (d. 570/1174-5 or possibly 571/1175-6) was orig
2 CONC inally a slave of Sultan Mahmud's vizier, al-Kamal al-Simirumi; then he passed into the possession of Sultan Mas'ud, who appointed him governor of Arran. For sometime he kept aloof from the quarrels over the sultanate, until the f
2 CONC ortunate marriage which he had made with Toghril's widow Mu'mine Khatun enabled him to champion the succession of Arslan b. Toghril; the latter he duly set up at Hamadan on the murder of Sulaiman-Shah in 556/1161. His son Nusrat a
2 CONC l-Din Pahlavan Muhammad was Sultan Arslans's half-brother, and Pahlavan succeeded not only to the paternal territories in Arran and much of Azerbaijan, but also to Jibal, Isfahan, and Ray, with his brother Qizil-Arslan 'Uthman rul
2 CONC ing in Tabriz as his subordinate. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * She is mentioned in the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ildeniz '''Wikipedia page'''] of her husband, Ildeniz:
2 CONT
2 CONT A Kipchak by origin, [Ildeniz] was formerly a freedman of Seljuq sultan Mehmed I's (1118-1131) vizier Kamal Din al-Simirumi and attained to the post of governor of Arran under Sultan Mas'ud (1134-1152). His raise as the most power
2 CONC ful peripheral emirs of the Seljuq empire was aided by the necessity of having a large army against the frequent incursions from the neighboring Kingdom of Georgia. He made himself virtually independent ruler of Azerbaijan by 1146
2 CONC . '''His marriage with the widow of Sultan Toghrul II (1132-1133; Masud’s brother and predecessor) afforded him to intervene in the dynastic strife which erupted upon Mas'ud’s death in 1152'''. He succeeded, in 1160, in deposing S
2 CONC ulayman Shah and installing his stepson Arslan b. Toghrul (1160-1175) as sultan. Conferred with the rank of atabek, Ildeniz now became a chief protector of the sultan’s authority.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * From the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Momine_Khatun_Mausoleum '''Wikipedia page'''] of the Momine Khatun Mausoleum:
2 CONT
2 CONT [The Momine Khatun Mausoleum] was commissioned by Ildegizid Atabeg Jahan Pahlawan (1175-1186), in honor of his first wife, Mu'mine Khatun, and completed in 1186-1187, as indicated on the Kufic-style inscriptive plaque above the en
2 CONC trance. Its architect, Adjemi ibn Abubekr (or Adjemi Nakchivani), also built the nearby mausoleum of Yusuf ibn Kuseyir. The mausoleum was probably originally built with a madrassa: drawings and photographs of the site from the nin
2 CONC eteenth century confirm that it existed as part of a religious and educational complex which no longer exists.
2 CONT
2 CONT * From the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eldiguzids '''Wikipedia page'''] of the Eldiguzids:
2 CONT
2 CONT Momine Khatun Mausoleum was commissioned by Ildegizid Atabeg Jahan Pahlawan in honor of his first wife, Mu'mine Khatun
