1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Initial information (her name, her father's name, and her grandfather's name) comes from [http://fabpedigree.com/s077/f081869.htm '''this site'''], and the rest of her family comes from [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedL
2 CONC ands/TURKS.htm#DhulNundied1174 '''Western Asia & North Africa (2)'''], a MedLands project, though it has been slightly edited to fit the format of a geni profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT GÜMÜŞTEKIN [Muhammad/Amir Ghazi] (-[1134/35]).  Vardan's History records that "the senior son Ghazi assumed authority" in 1104 after the death of his father[29].  Abul-Feda records that "Gumichtikin Ibn Tilou…Ibn ed-Danichmend" wa
2 CONC s sovereign of "Malatiya" in A.H. 492 (15 Jul 1099) and captured the Frankish leader[30].  He captured Caesarea, Sebastea and Amasea.  William of Tyre records that he defeated and killed Bohémond II Prince of Antioch, who had inva
2 CONC ded the territories of Leo I Lord of the Mountains [Armenia - Rupen] in Feb 1130, and had the prince's head embalmed and sent as a gift to the Caliph[31].  The Caliph and the Great Seljuk Sultan sent the insignia of king (malik) t
2 CONC o Gümüştekin in early 1135 and officially invested him with 'the northern country'[32].  Gümüştekin had five children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # MOHAMMED (-[Aug 1140/Oct 1143]).  He succeeded his father in 1135 as malik of Danişmend.  Abul-Feda records the death in A.H. 537 (1142/43) of "Mohammed ibn ed-Danichmend seigneur de Malatiya" after which his lands passed to "le
2 CONC  prince seldjoukide Mesoud fils de Kilidj-Arslan et souverain d'Icone"[33].  Mehmed had three children.
2 CONT #  ''' --- .  m MASUD I Seljuk Sultan of Rum, son of KILIC ARSLAN I Seljuk Sultan of Rum (-1155).''' 
2 CONT #  YAGHI ARSLAN (-[1164/65]).  Governor of Sivas 1141.  He and his brother rebelled against his nephew Dhu'l Nun[42].  The Chronicle of Patriarch Michel le Grand records that "Yakoub-Arslan" captured "Danoun [Dsoulnoun] fils de so
2 CONC n frère" who had rebelled "à Césarée"[43].  The Kamel-Altevarykh Chronicle records that "Kilidj Arslan, fils de Massoud prince de Conieh" defeated "Yaghi Arslan (fils de Kumuchtekin) fils de Danichment prince de Malatiah" after he
2 CONC  captured his wife "la fille d'Almelik Saltouk, fils d'Ali, fils d'Abou'l-Cassem" in A.H. 560 (1164/65), and married her to "son neveu Dhou'lnoun, fils de Mohammed"[44].  Yaghi Arslan had one child.
2 CONT # AYN al-DAWLA (-[1151]).  He rebelled against his brother Mehmed in the Jahan, but was driven out two years later and sought refuge with Joscelin Count of Edessa[45].  He ruled in Melitene 1141.  He and his brother rebelled again
2 CONC st his nephew Dhu'l Nun[46].  Ayn al-Dawla had one child: 
2 CONT # IBRAHIM .  Ibrahim had one child.
