2 CONT MASUD, son of Kilic ARSLAN I Seljuk Sultan of Rum (-[Apr] 1155, bur Iconium) m --- of Danishmend, daughter of GHAZI II Danishmend Emir.   Sultan Masud I had seven children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # ALP ARSLAN (-after 1145).  At Mosul.  He was deposed by Zengi in 1145.  
2 CONT # ---.  Ioannes Komnenos deserted to the Turks, converted to Islam in 1140, married the daughter of the Seljuk Sultan as his second wife[85], and became a noted scholar.  Niketas Choniates records the marriage of "Iohannes Isaacii
2 CONC  sebastocratoris filius" and "Masuti filiam"[86].  m (1140) as his second wife, IOANNES Komnenos Tzelepes, son of ISAAKIOS Komnenos caesar, & his wife --- (after 1114-[1145]).  One child: SULEIMAN Shah 
2 CONT #  --- .  m (1150) NUR ed-DIN of Aleppo and Damascus (-1174).  
2 CONT # KILIC ARSLAN (-end Aug 1192, bur Iconium).  Abul-Feda records the death in A.H. 551 (1156/57) of "le roi Mesoud, fils de Kilidj Arslan et souverain d'Icone…dans le pays d'Er-Roum" and the succession of "son fils Kilidj Arslan"[8
2 CONC 7].  He succeeded his father in 1155 as KILIC ARSLAN II Seljuk Sultan of Rum.  
2 CONT # son (-murdered 1155).  Smbat Sparapet's Chronicle records that Sultan Kilij Arslan had one of his brothers strangled after he was enthroned in [11 Feb 1155/10 Feb 1156][88].  
2 CONT # '''SHAHANSHAH (-after 1174).  His father installed him as ruler in Çankiri and Ankara but he rebelled against his brother after their father died[89].  Smbat Sparapet's Chronicle records that one of Sultan Kilij Arslan's brother
2 CONC s "fled to Gangra and Ankara" after his brother was enthroned in [11 Feb 1155/10 Feb 1156][90].  Abul-Feda records that "Chahanchah Ibn Medoud, frère de Kilidj Arslan" was granted sovereignty over "Ancouriya" in A.H. 560 (1164/65)
2 CONC [91].  He was deposed by Sultan Kilij Arslan II in 1169 and banished[92].  He fled to Constantinople in 1174[93].  m --- of Danishmend, daughter of ---.  The Chronicle of Patriarch Michel le Grand records that "Sehain Shah" marrie
2 CONC d "une princesse de la maison de Danischmend"[94]. ''' 
2 CONT # SANCAR-SHAH .  He received Ereğli under the division of territories organised by his brother Sultan Kilij Arslan II in [1186/87][95].  Sancar-Shah had one child: NIZAM al-DIN ARĞUN-SHAH .  He received Amasya under the division o
2 CONC f territories organised by his paternal uncle Sultan Kilij Arslan II in [1186/87][96]. 
