2 CONT # son (-murdered 1155).  Smbat Sparapet's Chronicle records that Sultan Kilij Arslan had one of his brothers strangled after he was enthroned in [11 Feb 1155/10 Feb 1156][88].  
2 CONT # SHAHANSHAH (-after 1174).  His father installed him as ruler in Çankiri and Ankara but he rebelled against his brother after their father died[89].  Smbat Sparapet's Chronicle records that one of Sultan Kilij Arslan's brothers "
2 CONC fled to Gangra and Ankara" after his brother was enthroned in [11 Feb 1155/10 Feb 1156][90].  Abul-Feda records that "Chahanchah Ibn Medoud, frère de Kilidj Arslan" was granted sovereignty over "Ancouriya" in A.H. 560 (1164/65)[91
2 CONC ].  He was deposed by Sultan Kilij Arslan II in 1169 and banished[92].  He fled to Constantinople in 1174[93].  m --- of Danishmend, daughter of ---.  The Chronicle of Patriarch Michel le Grand records that "Sehain Shah" married "
2 CONC une princesse de la maison de Danischmend"[94].  
2 CONT # SANCAR-SHAH .  He received Ereğli under the division of territories organised by his brother Sultan Kilij Arslan II in [1186/87][95].  Sancar-Shah had one child: NIZAM al-DIN ARĞUN-SHAH .  He received Amasya under the division o
2 CONC f territories organised by his paternal uncle Sultan Kilij Arslan II in [1186/87][96]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * from the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesud_I '''Wikipedia page'''] of her father, Ma'sud I of Rûm:
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Masud's daughters married John Tzelepes Komnenos, a member of the royal house of Byzantium who had converted to Islam.[4]
2 CONT
