2 CONT
2 CONT HISHAM (Córdoba 757-17 Apr 796). Ibn-el Kouthya records that "la fille de Youçouf" offered "une jeune esclave…Houlal" to Abd er-Rahman, adding that she became the mother of Hisham[55]. Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi records "…Hicham b. M
2 CONC ohammed b. Abd er-Rahman ed-Dakhil b. Moawiyya…" when reciting the ancestry of his remote descendant "El-Motadd billah" Emir of Córdoba[56]. Ibn-el Kouthya names "Soleiman et Hicham" as the two sons of Abd er-Rahman[57]. Appointed
2 CONC  Governor of Merida by his father. He arrived at Córdoba within days of his father's death, and was greeted as HISHAM I Emir of Córdoba. According to Arab sources, Emir Hisham was "passionate about the holy war", sending two armie
2 CONC s into battle in 791[58]. The first phase of the mosque at Córdoba was completed during the early part of his reign. He foiled a plot to depose him in favour of his cousin Muhammad al-Qasim in 805, which he repressed with great se
2 CONC verity. An uprising in Córdoba in 818 was also put down with extreme severity. The Chronicon Albeldense records that “Eiscam” reigned seven years and six months in Córdoba, adding in a later paragraph that he was the son of “Abder
2 CONC rhaman”[59]. [m] (a) ZOKHRUF, daughter of ---. Abd el-Wahid Merrakechi names "une concubine…Zokhrouf" as the mother of Emir Hakam I[60]. Hisham I & his concubine (a) had one child: al-HAKAM ([770/75]-822)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hisham_I_of_C%C3%B3rdoba
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hisham I de Córdoba (son of Abd Al Rahman I de Córdoba and Zaibra) was born 01 Mar 757, and died 28 Apr 796. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Notes for Hisham I de Córdoba: BIOGRAPHY: Subiu ao trono com 31 anos, tinha pele clara e cabelo ruivo. Esperto e enérgico, simples e piedoso.
2 CONT
2 CONT Acabou a edificação da mesquita iniciada pelo seu Pai.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hisham I de Córdoba are: +Al Hakam I de Córdoba, b. 770, d. 21 May 822.
