2 CONT Al-Rumayṣāʾ bint Milḥān (Arabic: الرميصاء بنت ملحان; died c. 650 CE; 28 AH), popularly known by her kunya as Umm Sulaym, was a follower or companion (Sahabiyyah) of Islamic prophet Muhammad and was one of the earliest women conver
2 CONC ts to Islam in Yathrib (now Medina).
