0 @N6000000002188182977@ NOTE Qusai ibn Kilab
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Qusai ibn Kilab ibn Murrah (Qusayy) (Arabic: ??? ??? ???? ??? ??????) (c.400–480) was the great-great-grandfather of Shaiba ibn Hashim (Abdul-Mutallib). He was fifth in the line of descent to Mohammad, and attained supreme power a
1 CONC t Mecca. Qusai is amongst the ancestors of Sahaba and the progenitor of the Banu Quraish [1].
1 CONT
1 CONT Also known as Zuhrah ibn Kilab ibn Murrah ibn Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy ibn Ghalib, he was born into the famous Quraysh tribe. When Qusai came of age, a man from the tribe of Banu Khuza'a named Hulail was the trustee of the Kaaba. Qusai mar
1 CONC ried his daughter and, according to Hulail's will, got the trusteeship of the Kaaba after him. He is reputed to have brought great honour and illustriousness to his tribe, due to his wisdom. He reconstructed the Kaaba from a state
1 CONC  of decay, and made the Arab people build their houses around it. He is known to have built the first "town hall" in the Arabian Peninsula. Leaders of different clans met in this hall to discuss their social, commercial, cultural 
1 CONC and political problems. A provident leader, Qusai created laws so that pilgrims who went to Mecca were supplied with food and water, which was paid for by a tax that he persuaded his people to pay.
1 CONT
1 CONT Qusai had just one son[citation needed], named Abd-al-Manaf ibn Qusai[citation needed].
1 CONT
1 CONT He was also the father of Abd-al-Uzza ibn Qusai [2].
1 CONT
1 CONT And also Abd-al-Dar ibn Qusai[3]
1 CONT
1 CONT According to some historians, Quraysh's real name was Fahr, and he was son of Malik son of Madar son of Kananah son of Khuzaimah son of Mudrikah son of Ilyas son of Mazar son of Nazar son of Ma`ad son of Adnan son of Isma`eel (Ish
1 CONC mael) son of Ibrahim (Abraham) son of Sam son of Noah[1]
0 @N6000000000437122906@ NOTE Name Suffix:<NSFX> Of The Khozaites
